# Template for release signing. Copy it, fill it in, and keep the copy out of Git.
#
#     copy keystore.properties.example keystore.properties
#
# `keystore.properties` is listed in .gitignore, as are `*.jks` and `*.keystore`, so neither this
# file's copy nor the keystore it points at can be committed by accident. Do not remove those lines
# to "fix" a build - that is how release keys end up in public repositories.
#
# Every value below can also be supplied as an environment variable, which is the better choice in
# CI and on a shared build machine because there is no second file to leak. The properties file wins
# where both are set.
#
#   storeFile      $KEYSTORE_PATH       relative paths are resolved against the project root
#   storePassword  $STORE_PASSWORD
#   keyAlias       $KEY_ALIAS
#   keyPassword    $KEY_PASSWORD
#
# To create the keystore, if you do not already have one:
#
#     keytool -genkeypair -v \
#       -keystore my-upload-key.jks \
#       -alias upload \
#       -keyalg RSA -keysize 2048 -validity 10000
#
# -validity 10000 is about 27 years, comfortably past the deadline Google Play enforces for a
# signing key. Choose both passwords yourself. There is no default, and no value belongs in a
# committed file.
#
# One thing keytool will tell you, so it is not a surprise later: modern keytool creates a PKCS12
# keystore, and PKCS12 cannot hold a key password different from the store password. keytool prints
# a warning and ignores -keypass, so keyPassword ends up equal to storePassword. That is fine for
# an upload key. If you specifically need two different passwords, add `-storetype JKS`.
#
# Note: the keystore and its passwords are what let you ship updates to an existing Play listing.
# Losing them means you cannot update the app without removing it and publishing under a new
# listing. Back the keystore up somewhere durable and separate from this machine, and keep the
# passwords somewhere you would not store the keystore itself.

storeFile=my-upload-key.jks
storePassword=
keyAlias=upload
keyPassword=